1
00:00:09,580 --> 00:00:12,920
Try stepping back and
looking at it in the light.

2
00:00:23,180 --> 00:00:28,620
An afternoon after the rain,
as if someone is calling out,

3
00:00:29,940 --> 00:00:35,280
walking while looking back,
my hand held by Mom.

4
00:00:36,160 --> 00:00:42,340
That mysterious feeling I had back then.

5
00:00:43,400 --> 00:00:47,700
So on the tiles of the arcade street,

6
00:00:47,700 --> 00:00:53,500
I tried walking only on the black ones.

7
00:00:55,900 --> 00:00:59,660
Everyone was a child once,

8
00:00:59,660 --> 00:01:01,820
but everyone has forgotten.

9
00:01:02,680 --> 00:01:09,080
Politicians with their self-important faces,
and the blue-eyeshadowed aunties too,

10
00:01:09,580 --> 00:01:14,660
Try turning at that corner over there.

11
00:01:15,680 --> 00:01:19,880
You can meet everyone, everyone.

12
00:01:22,080 --> 00:01:27,800
Over there is Kame-ari surely Kame-ari!

13
00:01:28,980 --> 00:01:33,060
Everyone, come on over to our town!

14
00:01:34,100 --> 00:01:34,560
Thank you.

15
00:01:36,900 --> 00:01:39,300
Wings of friendship.

16
00:01:51,160 --> 00:01:54,700
JAT Flight 421 is cruising smoothly.

17
00:01:54,700 --> 00:01:56,520
Passing PABBA.

18
00:01:57,940 --> 00:01:59,920
The approach airspace
for landing is clear skies.

19
00:01:59,920 --> 00:02:01,980
Radio, see you on the ground.

20
00:02:09,240 --> 00:02:10,660
Isn't that Reiko-san?

21
00:02:11,020 --> 00:02:14,580
Kei-chan! What a coincidence.
So we were on the same flight.

22
00:02:14,580 --> 00:02:15,820
I didn't notice.

23
00:02:16,700 --> 00:02:21,700
There was a 100th anniversary event
for the Nakagawa Group in Okinawa.

24
00:02:21,700 --> 00:02:22,700
And you, Reiko-san?

25
00:02:23,560 --> 00:02:25,880
I'm coming back from a friend's wedding.

26
00:02:29,160 --> 00:02:32,080
We will be arriving at
Haneda Airport shortly.

27
00:02:38,940 --> 00:02:40,620
Captain, the landing gear won't come out.

28
00:02:40,620 --> 00:02:41,140
What?

29
00:02:42,680 --> 00:02:43,400
Once more.

30
00:02:47,280 --> 00:02:48,520
No good, it won't come out.

31
00:02:48,520 --> 00:02:50,200
Abort landing, gain altitude.

32
00:02:53,240 --> 00:02:54,980
They're climbing again.

33
00:02:54,980 --> 00:02:56,720
I wonder what happened.

34
00:03:02,560 --> 00:03:05,420
What the... it's not flying at all!

35
00:03:05,420 --> 00:03:09,220
That's strange,
I built it exactly to the blueprint.

36
00:03:09,220 --> 00:03:11,360
The wing's position is wrong.

37
00:03:11,360 --> 00:03:12,320
Ryo-san.

38
00:03:12,320 --> 00:03:13,200
Let me have a look.

39
00:03:15,580 --> 00:03:18,140
Look, the center of
gravity is too far forward.

40
00:03:21,740 --> 00:03:23,980
What, the wing angle's all wrong too

41
00:03:24,640 --> 00:03:26,000
Is that right?

42
00:03:27,800 --> 00:03:29,640
The construction and placement
of the wings are what matter.

43
00:03:30,140 --> 00:03:32,160
Wings are the lifeblood of an airplane,
you know.

44
00:03:32,160 --> 00:03:35,360
Do you two know why airplanes fly?

45
00:03:36,720 --> 00:03:37,680
No idea.

46
00:03:37,680 --> 00:03:39,580
Because they fly, isn't it?

47
00:03:40,760 --> 00:03:44,920
By changing the angle of the wings
against the energy of the wind,

48
00:03:44,920 --> 00:03:47,920
drag and lift are generated,
and the plane rises into the air.

49
00:03:49,720 --> 00:03:52,240
Wow, Ryo-san, you really know everything!

50
00:03:52,940 --> 00:03:56,300
What I just said was secondhand,
from my best friend in elementary school.

51
00:03:57,800 --> 00:04:00,360
But for an elementary schooler
to know something like that,

52
00:04:00,410 --> 00:04:02,060
that's impressive,
that best friend of yours.

53
00:04:02,300 --> 00:04:05,410
Yeah. His name's Takashi-kun, you know.

54
00:04:05,460 --> 00:04:10,200
He loved airplanes so much that he said
he wanted to become a pilot someday.

55
00:04:11,900 --> 00:04:14,397
When I was your age,

56
00:04:14,447 --> 00:04:18,537
the model shop held a
flight contest every month.

57
00:04:18,587 --> 00:04:20,180
I entered it all the time.

58
00:04:20,820 --> 00:04:25,040
Do you know the Benten Hall on the island
in the middle of Shinobazu Pond in Ueno?

59
00:04:25,260 --> 00:04:25,620
Yeah.

60
00:04:26,040 --> 00:04:29,980
The contest was a race to fly your
plane all the way to Benten Hall,

61
00:04:29,980 --> 00:04:34,240
but it was tough. If your plane stalled along the way,
it would fall into the pond.

62
00:04:35,120 --> 00:04:36,380
Go, Stargo!

63
00:04:36,380 --> 00:04:37,000
Go!

64
00:04:37,000 --> 00:04:38,180
Go already!

65
00:04:41,200 --> 00:04:42,580
No. 21 is disqualified.

66
00:04:42,580 --> 00:04:43,480
Shit.

67
00:04:43,480 --> 00:04:45,020
Next, No. 22.

68
00:04:45,020 --> 00:04:45,760
Alright!

69
00:04:46,140 --> 00:04:48,520
Kankichi, do your best for us too!

70
00:04:48,520 --> 00:04:49,500
Count on you.

71
00:04:49,500 --> 00:04:51,240
Leave it to me.

72
00:04:52,300 --> 00:04:53,260
Direction, good.

73
00:04:54,880 --> 00:04:55,280
Good.

74
00:04:55,280 --> 00:04:56,160
Wind direction, good.

75
00:04:58,020 --> 00:04:58,820
Go!

76
00:04:58,880 --> 00:05:00,680
Hindenburg Gas!

77
00:05:05,920 --> 00:05:07,420
Entry 22 disqualified.

78
00:05:09,700 --> 00:05:11,440
It didn't even reach the pond.

79
00:05:11,440 --> 00:05:12,500
That's strange.

80
00:05:12,500 --> 00:05:14,140
What's wrong with it, I wonder?

81
00:05:14,140 --> 00:05:15,380
Is it everything?

82
00:05:17,000 --> 00:05:18,860
Looks like everyone else failed too.

83
00:05:18,860 --> 00:05:20,020
It's impossible.

84
00:05:20,020 --> 00:05:21,840
Flying all the way to Benten-dō?

85
00:05:22,360 --> 00:05:22,820
Amazing.

86
00:05:22,820 --> 00:05:23,660
Amazing.

87
00:05:23,660 --> 00:05:23,880
Incredible.

88
00:05:26,120 --> 00:05:26,580
Incredible.

89
00:05:27,740 --> 00:05:28,200
Wow.

90
00:05:28,810 --> 00:05:29,040
Wow.

91
00:05:29,040 --> 00:05:29,270
Unbelievable.

92
00:05:31,560 --> 00:05:32,020
Unbelievable.

93
00:05:32,020 --> 00:05:32,240
Amazing.

94
00:05:42,020 --> 00:05:42,480
Amazing!

95
00:05:45,280 --> 00:05:45,740
Amazing!

96
00:05:45,740 --> 00:05:46,320
Amazing!

97
00:05:46,320 --> 00:05:46,880
Amazing!

98
00:05:46,880 --> 00:05:47,380
Amazing!

99
00:05:47,380 --> 00:05:47,880
Amazing!

100
00:05:47,880 --> 00:05:48,720
Amazing!

101
00:05:48,720 --> 00:05:48,740
Amazing!

102
00:05:48,740 --> 00:05:49,380
Amazing!

103
00:05:49,380 --> 00:05:49,460
Amazing!

104
00:05:49,460 --> 00:05:49,540
Amazing!

105
00:05:49,540 --> 00:05:49,780
Incredible!

106
00:05:49,780 --> 00:05:49,800
Wow!

107
00:05:49,800 --> 00:05:49,820
That's amazing!

108
00:05:49,820 --> 00:05:49,840
So cool!

109
00:05:49,840 --> 00:05:49,860
Unbelievable!

110
00:05:49,860 --> 00:05:49,880
Whoa, that's something!

111
00:05:50,020 --> 00:05:50,800
It's number 24!

112
00:05:50,800 --> 00:05:52,260
Number 24?

113
00:05:56,880 --> 00:05:59,440
They're just kids, like us.

114
00:06:00,280 --> 00:06:03,960
The winner is Asahina Takashi-kun,
with the Lindbergh.

115
00:06:03,960 --> 00:06:06,540
Wow, that plane is amazing.

116
00:06:07,080 --> 00:06:08,560
I can't believe it.

117
00:06:08,560 --> 00:06:11,920
Hey, would you mind
teaching me how to make one?

118
00:06:12,240 --> 00:06:12,700
Please.

119
00:06:14,000 --> 00:06:14,680
Sure.

120
00:06:14,680 --> 00:06:16,020
Yay!

121
00:06:18,220 --> 00:06:21,940
For model planes, making the wings and
placing them correctly is what matters.

122
00:06:22,400 --> 00:06:24,080
The wings are the lifeblood of a plane,
you know.

123
00:06:25,900 --> 00:06:27,800
Do you know why planes fly?

124
00:06:27,920 --> 00:06:30,580
Well isn't it because
they fly that they fly?

125
00:06:31,180 --> 00:06:35,180
By changing the angle of the wings
against the energy of the wind,

126
00:06:35,180 --> 00:06:38,140
drag and lift are generated,
and the plane floats.

127
00:06:39,200 --> 00:06:39,560
What about lift?

128
00:06:39,840 --> 00:06:40,700
Lift?

129
00:06:40,920 --> 00:06:41,780
Lift?

130
00:06:42,640 --> 00:06:43,600
It's hard, isn't it.

131
00:06:44,140 --> 00:06:48,380
Airflow has the property that as its speed increases,
air pressure drops.

132
00:06:48,980 --> 00:06:53,060
The reason the wing is stretched only over
the top is to create a pressure difference.

133
00:06:53,060 --> 00:06:53,840
Got it?

134
00:06:54,000 --> 00:06:55,180
You get it, right?

135
00:06:55,180 --> 00:06:56,200
You don't get it, do you?

136
00:06:56,200 --> 00:06:56,720
In short,

137
00:06:56,720 --> 00:07:00,820
For once,
Kankichi's brought a smart friend over.

138
00:07:00,820 --> 00:07:03,500
Don't be an idiot,
you shouldn't say things like that.

139
00:07:04,280 --> 00:07:06,060
A rice cracker would've been fine too.

140
00:07:06,060 --> 00:07:07,220
Auntie, thank you very much.

141
00:07:07,940 --> 00:07:09,040
Auntie?

142
00:07:09,220 --> 00:07:12,700
Oh my, calling me "auntie" like that!

143
00:07:13,740 --> 00:07:16,280
Don't laugh like that, it's creepy.

144
00:07:16,780 --> 00:07:17,580
Hee hee.

145
00:07:17,580 --> 00:07:18,920
Well, take your time.

146
00:07:20,580 --> 00:07:21,840
What a well-mannered child.

147
00:07:22,240 --> 00:07:24,300
Smart kids really are different,
aren't they.

148
00:07:25,360 --> 00:07:27,800
What's with the
"ho-ho-ho"? Who's the idiot here?

149
00:07:28,240 --> 00:07:31,220
Takashi, even though he's an
elementary schooler like us,

150
00:07:31,220 --> 00:07:33,200
you know such difficult things.

151
00:07:33,200 --> 00:07:36,140
Hey, my dream is to become a pilot.

152
00:07:36,140 --> 00:07:37,340
A pilot?

153
00:07:37,560 --> 00:07:38,540
That's cool.

154
00:07:38,540 --> 00:07:40,140
So that's why you know so much about it.

155
00:07:40,500 --> 00:07:41,080
Well, yeah.

156
00:07:43,640 --> 00:07:45,480
What's that sparkly thing?

157
00:07:46,040 --> 00:07:47,600
What do you mean? It's a menko, isn't it?

158
00:07:47,600 --> 00:07:50,280
Takashi, don't you know what a menko is?

159
00:07:50,440 --> 00:07:51,040
Menko?

160
00:07:51,580 --> 00:07:53,580
Then I'll teach you how to play.

161
00:07:54,260 --> 00:07:57,920
Like this, you set down your
menko and hook your foot over it.

162
00:08:03,400 --> 00:08:05,420
You get to take the menko
that were flipped over.

163
00:08:05,420 --> 00:08:08,220
Wow, but what a sound that makes!

164
00:08:08,220 --> 00:08:11,020
It takes three years to get that sound.

165
00:08:12,000 --> 00:08:13,660
Whoa, that's impressive.

166
00:08:13,660 --> 00:08:19,140
Among menko, these silver picture ones are called ginmen,
and they're valuable.

167
00:08:19,600 --> 00:08:23,240
Wow, Kankichi has 200 silver ones!

168
00:08:23,240 --> 00:08:25,340
It's a man's badge of honor, you know.

169
00:08:25,340 --> 00:08:28,020
Kankichi, you're good at this, aren't you?

170
00:08:28,020 --> 00:08:28,920
Well, yeah.

171
00:08:28,920 --> 00:08:31,440
In Asakusa, Kankichi is the strongest.

172
00:08:33,240 --> 00:08:37,180
He's even done the cross throw so many
times he's dislocated his shoulder.

173
00:08:37,180 --> 00:08:38,860
Shut up.

174
00:08:38,860 --> 00:08:40,840
It's a really hardcore game

175
00:08:40,840 --> 00:08:42,640
Will you teach me?

176
00:08:42,940 --> 00:08:43,720
Sure, why not.

177
00:08:50,480 --> 00:08:51,940
It's no good at all.

178
00:08:52,440 --> 00:08:54,520
Dig in harder on your pivot foot.

179
00:08:55,040 --> 00:08:55,460
Like this?

180
00:08:55,760 --> 00:08:56,820
After that, it's all about spirit.

181
00:08:56,820 --> 00:09:00,060
For example,
think back to when you got scolded

182
00:09:00,060 --> 00:09:02,280
you idiot, Dad!

183
00:09:03,160 --> 00:09:03,800
What?

184
00:09:06,020 --> 00:09:08,740
since saying it out loud can be dangerous,

185
00:09:09,200 --> 00:09:12,980
scream it silently in your heart
and slam the menko down all at once.

186
00:09:12,980 --> 00:09:13,760
Got it.

187
00:09:14,680 --> 00:09:17,440
You idiot, Papa!

188
00:09:18,180 --> 00:09:20,380
Yay, you did it, Kankichi-kun!

189
00:09:20,960 --> 00:09:22,260
Way to go, Takashi-kun!

190
00:09:23,880 --> 00:09:26,180
Since then, we've gone to different schools,

191
00:09:27,180 --> 00:09:29,560
and Takashi played with me almost every day,

192
00:09:30,020 --> 00:09:31,820
and we spent our days absorbed
in menko and model planes.

193
00:09:34,400 --> 00:09:35,320
Lost again.

194
00:09:35,800 --> 00:09:36,740
Yes, got it!

195
00:09:41,320 --> 00:09:42,760
Yes, our chance, Takashi!

196
00:09:43,580 --> 00:09:46,300
I knew it,
I'm still not ready for real battles.

197
00:09:46,700 --> 00:09:49,020
If I keep taking Kankichi's menko like this,

198
00:09:49,020 --> 00:09:50,260
never mind, don't worry about it.

199
00:09:50,740 --> 00:09:54,280
Takashi, the secret to winning
at menko is never giving up.

200
00:09:54,780 --> 00:09:58,260
If you don't give up and believe you'll definitely win,
you'll surely win.

201
00:09:58,260 --> 00:10:00,380
Okay, Kankichi.

202
00:10:04,920 --> 00:10:07,860
If you don't give up and believe you'll definitely win,
you'll surely win.

203
00:10:08,520 --> 00:10:09,620
Alright, bababa-ro!

204
00:10:09,620 --> 00:10:10,780
Idiot!

205
00:10:18,280 --> 00:10:19,200
Yay!

206
00:10:19,200 --> 00:10:20,660
Wow, yay!

207
00:10:20,660 --> 00:10:21,300
We did it!

208
00:10:23,920 --> 00:10:27,360
Hey, come visit my house sometime too.

209
00:10:27,360 --> 00:10:30,280
It's in Nogata 1-chome,
near Tokyo University.

210
00:10:30,720 --> 00:10:32,260
Can I really go?

211
00:10:32,700 --> 00:10:33,100
Yeah.

212
00:10:33,580 --> 00:10:35,020
All right, let's go!

213
00:10:35,780 --> 00:10:39,280
Here it is.

214
00:10:39,280 --> 00:10:40,860
Look, it's an American car!

215
00:10:40,860 --> 00:10:43,360
As expected,
a rich man's house is different!

216
00:10:44,500 --> 00:10:45,580
Welcome.

217
00:10:46,300 --> 00:10:47,100
Um...

218
00:10:47,100 --> 00:10:47,840
Hello.

219
00:10:48,960 --> 00:10:50,240
Please, come in.

220
00:10:51,300 --> 00:10:52,160
Let's go to my room.

221
00:10:52,650 --> 00:10:53,840
I'll bring some tea.

222
00:10:54,420 --> 00:10:56,060
I'll bring you some tea later, dear.

223
00:10:56,060 --> 00:10:56,660
Yes.

224
00:10:57,060 --> 00:10:57,980
It's beautiful, isn't it.

225
00:10:57,980 --> 00:10:58,940
And it's so elegant.

226
00:10:59,340 --> 00:11:01,420
That's nothing like my mom.

227
00:11:01,880 --> 00:11:03,520
What's wrong? Hurry up and come in.

228
00:11:03,520 --> 00:11:07,460
Wow, that's amazing.

229
00:11:07,980 --> 00:11:10,320
Takashi, your room is full of airplanes.

230
00:11:10,920 --> 00:11:12,240
My dad's a pilot.

231
00:11:12,780 --> 00:11:14,020
A pilot?

232
00:11:14,020 --> 00:11:16,100
So that's why you dream of becoming a pilot.

233
00:11:16,580 --> 00:11:17,260
That's amazing.

234
00:11:18,860 --> 00:11:19,200
Yes.

235
00:11:19,600 --> 00:11:20,860
The tea's ready.

236
00:11:21,300 --> 00:11:22,360
Sorry about that.

237
00:11:26,480 --> 00:11:28,140
Here, it's coffee.

238
00:11:28,140 --> 00:11:29,300
Sugar?

239
00:11:30,700 --> 00:11:34,280
Since it's my first time having coffee,
about ten cubes.

240
00:11:34,280 --> 00:11:36,080
Us too, ten.

241
00:11:36,980 --> 00:11:37,740
Ten cubes?

242
00:11:38,280 --> 00:11:39,560
Welcome.

243
00:11:40,060 --> 00:11:40,969
Dad,

244
00:11:41,019 --> 00:11:44,280
these are the friends of Sakusa's
I told you about the other day.

245
00:11:44,280 --> 00:11:45,880
So you're the ones.

246
00:11:45,880 --> 00:11:47,120
Thank you for having us.

247
00:11:47,120 --> 00:11:49,280
Dad, are you going out already?

248
00:11:49,280 --> 00:11:53,120
Yes, this time it's a flight to Europe,
so it'll be a long one.

249
00:11:53,120 --> 00:11:55,700
Apparently it's a cool Europe.

250
00:11:55,700 --> 00:11:56,880
Europe

251
00:11:57,740 --> 00:11:59,380
Where's Europe?

252
00:11:59,380 --> 00:12:01,120
I know Harappa.

253
00:12:01,120 --> 00:12:02,380
Well, make yourselves at home.

254
00:12:02,380 --> 00:12:03,540
Thanks.

255
00:12:03,540 --> 00:12:04,720
Have a safe trip.

256
00:12:05,260 --> 00:12:06,980
Are you going in the car downstairs?

257
00:12:06,980 --> 00:12:09,560
The dad I saw on TV knows everything, right?

258
00:12:09,560 --> 00:12:10,520
Just like Dad.

259
00:12:10,520 --> 00:12:13,040
It's like an American family sitcom.

260
00:12:13,040 --> 00:12:14,140
What's wrong?

261
00:12:14,760 --> 00:12:17,780
No, a father who goes to
work wearing a necktie,

262
00:12:19,280 --> 00:12:20,299
my old man,

263
00:12:20,349 --> 00:12:23,380
well, your father's always
in his dressing gown,

264
00:12:23,380 --> 00:12:25,360
mine too, mine's inside out.

265
00:12:26,060 --> 00:12:30,460
I hear your family's an established business in Asakusa.
How lovely.

266
00:12:31,240 --> 00:12:33,620
Not at all, it's just old and rundown.

267
00:12:33,620 --> 00:12:36,400
All three of the old men are heavy drinkers,
you know.

268
00:12:36,400 --> 00:12:39,280
Neckties only come out for
memorial services, right?

269
00:12:39,280 --> 00:12:39,805
Well,

270
00:12:39,855 --> 00:12:43,500
then please make yourselves
at home and take your time.

271
00:12:43,500 --> 00:12:45,160
Yes, thank you.

272
00:12:48,340 --> 00:12:50,220
Lucky you, Takashi.

273
00:12:50,220 --> 00:12:54,380
With a pretty mom and a cool dad like that.

274
00:12:54,380 --> 00:12:55,660
Pretty jealous

275
00:12:57,120 --> 00:12:59,960
I'm more jealous of you,
Kankichi, and the others.

276
00:13:01,500 --> 00:13:03,680
Right. Shall we play a game or something?

277
00:13:04,620 --> 00:13:06,240
Wow, so many games!

278
00:13:07,040 --> 00:13:08,000
Which one should we pick?

279
00:13:08,000 --> 00:13:10,180
The timetable train-guessing game?

280
00:13:10,500 --> 00:13:12,240
What's fun about that?

281
00:13:12,240 --> 00:13:14,260
Chinkichi is a total train nut.

282
00:13:15,160 --> 00:13:17,840
Come on, just once. It's fun, I promise.

283
00:13:18,000 --> 00:13:19,540
You play it alone.

284
00:13:32,160 --> 00:13:34,280
What? You want me to wear a tie?

285
00:13:35,780 --> 00:13:37,260
Do you have a fever or something?

286
00:13:37,640 --> 00:13:38,200
No, I don't.

287
00:13:38,780 --> 00:13:41,740
Dad, be like Takashi's dad and wear a tie.

288
00:13:42,200 --> 00:13:44,140
Can you make stew while wearing a tie?

289
00:13:44,620 --> 00:13:45,120
Idiot.

290
00:13:45,120 --> 00:13:45,580
Just leave it.

291
00:13:46,360 --> 00:13:49,140
Kankichi, the coffee's ready.

292
00:13:49,140 --> 00:13:51,700
Impressive, this makes it just like America.

293
00:13:52,480 --> 00:13:53,200
Here you go.

294
00:13:55,540 --> 00:13:57,280
Mom, not in a teacup,

295
00:13:57,280 --> 00:13:59,380
we drink from those cups with handles.

296
00:13:59,780 --> 00:14:01,360
We don't have anything like that at home.

297
00:14:01,360 --> 00:14:03,320
Once it's in your stomach,
it's all the same.

298
00:14:05,580 --> 00:14:09,260
No way,
this old man is a far cry from America.

299
00:14:10,760 --> 00:14:13,780
What? You want me to
get a pilot's license now?

300
00:14:14,220 --> 00:14:16,120
Don't talk such nonsense.

301
00:14:16,120 --> 00:14:17,820
What are you thinking?

302
00:14:17,820 --> 00:14:20,040
If you have time to think about that,

303
00:14:20,040 --> 00:14:22,080
you should learn a little
about making paper lanterns.

304
00:14:22,080 --> 00:14:23,960
We won't make the orders in time, you know.

305
00:14:23,960 --> 00:14:24,700
Geez.

306
00:14:26,280 --> 00:14:28,140
What? He's the one for the next audition?

307
00:14:28,320 --> 00:14:30,500
It's cooler to make deliveries by car.

308
00:14:30,500 --> 00:14:31,840
You idiot.

309
00:14:31,840 --> 00:14:34,080
Where would we get that kind of money?

310
00:14:36,060 --> 00:14:37,400
Damn my old man!

311
00:14:39,260 --> 00:14:39,360
No way!

312
00:14:39,680 --> 00:14:41,920
My old man's hopeless to talk to too.

313
00:14:41,920 --> 00:14:44,800
All three of them are stubborn as rocks,
you know.

314
00:14:45,280 --> 00:14:47,400
Honestly, Takashi, I envy you.

315
00:14:47,860 --> 00:14:49,740
A fancy house and an expensive car.

316
00:14:49,740 --> 00:14:52,240
A beautiful mom and a handsome dad.

317
00:14:52,240 --> 00:14:53,240
Must be nice.

318
00:14:54,580 --> 00:14:55,740
That's not true.

319
00:14:56,100 --> 00:14:58,640
Dad's hardly ever home because of work.

320
00:14:59,280 --> 00:15:02,980
I envy you, Kankichi-kun, and everyone
else whose parents are always together.

321
00:15:02,980 --> 00:15:04,880
Saying it's just unbearably noisy.

322
00:15:04,880 --> 00:15:05,320
Yeah, exactly.

323
00:15:05,320 --> 00:15:05,460
Yeah.

324
00:15:06,680 --> 00:15:11,360
My dad and mom don't seem
to get along very well.

325
00:15:11,360 --> 00:15:13,020
No way.

326
00:15:14,460 --> 00:15:18,080
Mom and Dad have been fighting a lot lately.

327
00:15:18,720 --> 00:15:20,620
We don't need to live in a fancy house.

328
00:15:21,200 --> 00:15:23,040
We don't even need an expensive car.

329
00:15:23,420 --> 00:15:26,260
As long as Mom and Dad get along,

330
00:15:27,060 --> 00:15:28,240
I won't worry.

331
00:15:28,240 --> 00:15:31,780
My old man and my old lady fight every single day,
you know.

332
00:15:31,780 --> 00:15:33,020
Same at our place.

333
00:15:33,020 --> 00:15:33,880
Us too.

334
00:15:35,320 --> 00:15:38,420
Takashi,
your mom and dad will make up eventually.

335
00:15:38,420 --> 00:15:39,240
You think so?

336
00:15:39,640 --> 00:15:40,620
They're grown-ups, after all.

337
00:15:40,620 --> 00:15:42,800
That's right. It'll be fine.

338
00:15:49,820 --> 00:15:51,700
Yeah, your balance has gotten a lot better.

339
00:15:52,120 --> 00:15:52,780
Really?

340
00:15:53,180 --> 00:15:55,240
Takashi-kun praised me, amazing!

341
00:15:56,580 --> 00:15:58,940
Alright,
this month's flying contest is in the bag.

342
00:15:58,940 --> 00:16:00,820
That's what you say right
before you fall in the pond.

343
00:16:01,360 --> 00:16:02,020
What did you say?

344
00:16:02,160 --> 00:16:04,100
But you might actually
get a pretty good result.

345
00:16:05,320 --> 00:16:07,660
Maybe I'll try flying it inside the
movie theater we're going to next week.

346
00:16:07,660 --> 00:16:09,080
Cut it out, Kankichi.

347
00:16:09,080 --> 00:16:09,980
Next week

348
00:16:09,980 --> 00:16:11,180
Looking forward to it.

349
00:16:18,220 --> 00:16:20,260
Do you really hate being
with your family that much?

350
00:16:20,260 --> 00:16:21,700
Enough already, won't you?

351
00:16:21,700 --> 00:16:24,920
You're always working, working, working.

352
00:16:25,300 --> 00:16:27,220
Which is more important to you,
family or work?

353
00:16:27,840 --> 00:16:29,660
And you have a flight coming up.

354
00:16:29,660 --> 00:16:31,460
And you call yourself a pilot's wife?

355
00:16:31,460 --> 00:16:34,520
You should have just married your airplane.

356
00:16:43,840 --> 00:16:44,780
He's really late

357
00:16:45,160 --> 00:16:46,740
The movie's going to start soon!

358
00:16:49,060 --> 00:16:50,280
Hey, it's starting!

359
00:16:50,280 --> 00:16:52,320
Yeah, let's wait inside.

360
00:16:55,340 --> 00:16:57,500
Takashi didn't come after all

361
00:16:57,500 --> 00:16:58,960
Maybe he went to cram school?

362
00:16:59,480 --> 00:17:01,380
At least let's give him the pamphlet.

363
00:17:01,380 --> 00:17:03,720
Takashi was really looking forward to the movie,
after all.

364
00:17:03,720 --> 00:17:05,620
Hey, Takashi's house...

365
00:17:09,120 --> 00:17:10,120
It's pitch black.

366
00:17:10,120 --> 00:17:11,540
That's strange.

367
00:17:11,540 --> 00:17:13,220
Nobody's answering at all.

368
00:17:13,980 --> 00:17:15,360
The car's gone too.

369
00:17:15,360 --> 00:17:17,940
Are you the Kankichi and the others?

370
00:17:18,440 --> 00:17:19,620
Yes, that's us.

371
00:17:19,620 --> 00:17:23,440
I've been asked to hold
this for Asana's son.

372
00:17:25,140 --> 00:17:26,660
Takashi's plane!

373
00:17:26,660 --> 00:17:27,420
Thank you.

374
00:17:27,420 --> 00:17:29,880
There's a letter attached.

375
00:17:29,880 --> 00:17:31,840
Uncle, what about Takashi and the others?

376
00:17:31,840 --> 00:17:33,720
They've moved out.

377
00:17:33,720 --> 00:17:35,520
His parents got divorced.

378
00:17:36,320 --> 00:17:37,000
Divorce!

379
00:17:37,000 --> 00:17:39,620
They just left with his mother a moment ago.

380
00:17:39,620 --> 00:17:42,280
They're probably going back
to their hometown of Aomori.

381
00:17:42,780 --> 00:17:45,140
That's why they left without telling us.

382
00:17:47,500 --> 00:17:50,880
Kankichi, Tonpei, Chinkichi...

383
00:17:51,340 --> 00:17:53,420
Please forgive me for
leaving without a word.

384
00:17:53,940 --> 00:17:57,200
How much fun the two months
I spent with you guys were.

385
00:18:01,160 --> 00:18:03,900
The 22:00 Hatsukari
train from Ueno to Aomori.

386
00:18:03,900 --> 00:18:05,480
It's probably this train.

387
00:18:06,320 --> 00:18:06,620
12:00?

388
00:18:06,740 --> 00:18:08,240
Five minutes until departure!

389
00:18:08,360 --> 00:18:12,800
No way! It takes at least 10 minutes from here to Ueno Station!
We won't make it!

390
00:18:18,540 --> 00:18:19,860
No, we can still make it!

391
00:18:20,480 --> 00:18:21,320
No way!

392
00:18:22,280 --> 00:18:26,190
The 22:00 Hatsukari express bound
for Aomori is about to depart.

393
00:18:26,240 --> 00:18:30,380
Passengers, please board and wait.

394
00:18:30,380 --> 00:18:30,480
Yes.

395
00:18:34,440 --> 00:18:36,100
Kankichi, it's impossible.

396
00:18:36,100 --> 00:18:37,180
We won't make it.

397
00:18:37,180 --> 00:18:39,040
Besides, you're going the wrong way!

398
00:18:39,040 --> 00:18:40,300
Sorry.

399
00:18:41,100 --> 00:18:42,260
I'll stop by home.

400
00:18:42,260 --> 00:18:43,120
Wait for me.

401
00:18:46,840 --> 00:18:47,840
Kankichi.

402
00:18:48,340 --> 00:18:50,000
What are you thinking?

403
00:18:53,140 --> 00:18:54,940
Will you be okay without Dad?

404
00:18:55,240 --> 00:18:55,880
Takashi.

405
00:18:56,380 --> 00:18:57,340
Yes, Mom.

406
00:19:05,000 --> 00:19:06,140
It just left.

407
00:19:06,920 --> 00:19:08,080
It's hopeless.

408
00:19:08,080 --> 00:19:08,700
Hey.

409
00:19:11,920 --> 00:19:14,020
What are you doing? The train's already...

410
00:19:14,020 --> 00:19:14,640
Hey.

411
00:19:16,660 --> 00:19:18,800
It's no use, we won't make it now.

412
00:19:18,800 --> 00:19:21,780
And where are you going?
Ueno Station is that way!

413
00:19:21,780 --> 00:19:23,460
Just follow me.

414
00:19:23,460 --> 00:19:26,240
They seemed so happy, so why...

415
00:19:26,240 --> 00:19:29,080
Why on earth did they get divorced,
Kankichi?

416
00:19:30,380 --> 00:19:32,080
Adult-world matters like that...

417
00:19:32,080 --> 00:19:34,380
Damn it, damn it, damn it!

418
00:19:42,340 --> 00:19:43,160
Goodbye.

419
00:19:53,320 --> 00:19:55,000
I see, the Tachibashi in Nippori

420
00:19:55,000 --> 00:19:56,560
If we're here, the train will pass through.

421
00:19:57,000 --> 00:19:58,000
What time is it now?

422
00:19:59,440 --> 00:20:00,400
10:05.

423
00:20:01,580 --> 00:20:03,100
There it is, that train!

424
00:20:07,340 --> 00:20:08,260
Help me.

425
00:20:10,420 --> 00:20:11,060
Ginga.

426
00:20:11,060 --> 00:20:14,100
Did you go to get this?
What are we going to do with this?

427
00:20:14,100 --> 00:20:17,280
Takashi gave us his most precious airplane.

428
00:20:17,840 --> 00:20:19,380
Now it's my turn.

429
00:20:21,480 --> 00:20:22,940
Throw it at the train!

430
00:20:29,540 --> 00:20:31,640
Take this treasure.

431
00:20:39,460 --> 00:20:40,600
It's just snow.

432
00:20:40,600 --> 00:20:42,460
There's shiny paper flying!

433
00:20:47,300 --> 00:20:48,380
No way.

434
00:20:50,880 --> 00:20:52,440
Kankichi and the others.

435
00:20:52,440 --> 00:20:54,540
Let's fly the airplane together again.

436
00:20:54,540 --> 00:20:55,960
We'll definitely do it!

437
00:21:09,500 --> 00:21:11,300
He was on board, Takashi-kun.

438
00:21:11,300 --> 00:21:11,700
There he is.

439
00:21:11,700 --> 00:21:13,700
Thank goodness, we caught up.

440
00:21:14,400 --> 00:21:14,800
Yeah.

441
00:21:21,600 --> 00:21:23,520
Wow, amazing!

442
00:21:24,300 --> 00:21:25,420
Ryo-san, thank you.

443
00:21:27,240 --> 00:21:31,020
Ryo-san,
so did that Takashi-kun become a pilot?

444
00:21:31,640 --> 00:21:34,116
Who knows, but I believe he did.

445
00:21:34,166 --> 00:21:37,184
I'm sure he made his dream
of becoming a pilot come true,

446
00:21:37,234 --> 00:21:39,220
and is flying through
the skies of the world.

447
00:21:39,600 --> 00:21:41,357
Ryo-san, it's bad!

448
00:21:41,407 --> 00:21:44,660
It's the plane Reiko and Nakagawa are on!

449
00:21:46,320 --> 00:21:49,128
Attention passengers,
due to unavoidable circumstances,

450
00:21:49,178 --> 00:21:51,680
we will now make a belly landing.

451
00:21:52,180 --> 00:21:55,160
Please stay calm and follow the
instructions of the cabin crew.

452
00:21:55,620 --> 00:21:56,380
Everyone, please calm down.

453
00:21:56,680 --> 00:21:59,033
Shouting here won't accomplish anything.

454
00:21:59,083 --> 00:22:00,820
Let's trust the captain.

455
00:22:08,960 --> 00:22:12,280
Don't give up. If you believe you'll absolutely win,
you will surely win.

456
00:22:12,820 --> 00:22:15,640
Kankichi, I won't give up.

457
00:22:22,500 --> 00:22:23,300
Here it comes!

458
00:23:00,100 --> 00:23:02,300
Captain, we did it! It's a success!

459
00:23:14,300 --> 00:23:14,980
Reikon

460
00:23:14,980 --> 00:23:15,680
Nakagawa

461
00:23:16,300 --> 00:23:17,500
Ryo-chan

462
00:23:17,500 --> 00:23:18,300
Senpai

463
00:23:18,300 --> 00:23:19,180
Terai-san

464
00:23:19,700 --> 00:23:20,860
You're safe, then.

465
00:23:20,860 --> 00:23:23,000
Thanks to you, we were saved.

466
00:23:23,000 --> 00:23:24,100
I'm glad.

467
00:23:24,100 --> 00:23:27,340
It's thanks to the captain's calm piloting.

468
00:23:27,340 --> 00:23:27,860
It's the captain.

469
00:23:41,460 --> 00:23:42,460
Kankichi-kun

470
00:23:47,780 --> 00:23:49,220
Takashi-kun

471
00:24:07,420 --> 00:24:13,940
Once I've drawn my eyebrows,
it's a dash, dash, dash to the station!

472
00:24:13,940 --> 00:24:19,560
A quick nap on the train,
leaning against the back of the seat.

473
00:24:20,620 --> 00:24:25,860
Another hard week,
your exhaustion is only natural.

474
00:24:27,020 --> 00:24:30,560
But you look so cool with
one hand in your pocket.

475
00:24:30,560 --> 00:24:33,300
Beef bowl, extra sauce, extra soggy.

476
00:24:33,300 --> 00:24:36,480
Even the irritation from endless overtime,

477
00:24:37,040 --> 00:24:40,240
melts away, all cleared up.

478
00:24:43,560 --> 00:24:46,340
Every day is no problem.

479
00:24:46,340 --> 00:24:50,020
Once you step under a hot shower,

480
00:24:50,020 --> 00:24:53,040
Every day is no problem.

481
00:24:53,040 --> 00:24:56,600
A sleep pillow restores your energy.

482
00:24:59,760 --> 00:25:02,540
Every day is no problem

483
00:25:03,460 --> 00:25:06,200
I love a girl like me

484
00:25:06,200 --> 00:25:09,420
Every day is no brain

485
00:25:09,420 --> 00:25:13,040
Monday with hearts flying around

486
00:25:13,040 --> 00:25:17,460
Andy, Andy, no brain

487
00:25:19,480 --> 00:25:22,740
Denkyoku Plus! Long time no see.

488
00:25:22,740 --> 00:25:24,960
Going to the amusement park with your dad

489
00:25:24,960 --> 00:25:27,920
Since he's your father,
I wondered what kind of guy he'd be,

490
00:25:27,920 --> 00:25:30,740
but he turns out to be pretty normal,
doesn't he?

491
00:25:30,740 --> 00:25:33,300
Hey, do something about it, old man!

492
00:25:33,300 --> 00:25:37,320
Next time, the Hyper President's
family service, count on it.

493
00:25:45,520 --> 00:25:49,240
Everyone, come on over to our town!

